homa City-area district that leans Republican by nine points. She has raised nearly $2 million and holds about $2 million on hand, while Democratic nominee Jena Nelson has raised under $450,000 with little cash remaining. No independent spending has appeared on either side.\n\nAll nine expert ratings put the race at Safe or Solid Republican, and prediction markets price Nelson's chances around one in ten. A leaked-audio story about Bice and Trump is the only notable negative, but it has not altered the race's fundamentals. The expected outcome is a comfortable Bice win in the low double digits.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0366, "margin": -12.0}]}